<LegalPage
  title="Man of the Match: Voting Rules"
  tag="Man of the Match"
  description="How fan voting for the Lobi Stars FC Man of the Match works."
  updated="9 October 2026"
>
  <h2>Who can vote</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Anyone with a free Lobi Stars fan account and a confirmed email address.</li>
    <li>One account per person.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When you can vote</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Voting runs for <strong>Lobi Stars home games only</strong>.</li>
    <li>Voting <strong>opens at kick-off</strong> and <strong>closes at full time</strong>. If the club doesn't record the final whistle, voting closes automatically 2 hours 15 minutes after kick-off.</li>
    <li>All times are taken from the club's server clock in Nigerian time (WAT), not from your device.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to vote</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Open the match's Matchday Live page and choose the <strong>Vote MOTM</strong> tab.</li>
    <li>You can vote for one <strong>Lobi Stars player</strong> from that match's squad (starting XI and substitutes).</li>
    <li><strong>One vote per account per match.</strong> Votes cannot be changed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Results</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>During the match only the number of fans who have voted is shown, not how many votes each player has.</li>
    <li>At full time the results are revealed: every player's votes and percentage. The player with the most votes is the Man of the Match. If players are level on votes, they are joint winners.</li>
    <li>Each player's total of Man of the Match awards is shown on their profile.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Fair play</h2>
  <p>The club may remove votes it reasonably believes come from fake or duplicate accounts. The club's decision is final. Your personal data is used as described in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
  <p><a href="/man-of-the-match/">&larr; Back to Man of the Match</a></p>
</LegalPage>
